<p>Second, -1 is objectively four different personalities. They refer to themselves by separate names and each has a consitent behavior pattern that is markedly distinct from the others. Wether these personalities are part of a single entity (the ghostly equivalent of multiple personality disorder) or are 4 separate things that happen to time-share a magic walkie-talkie is irrelevant. The fact that the research team has formed competing schools of opinion on the matter has no place in what is ostensibly a formal briefing.</p>

