			<div class="content" id="post-content-1494312">
									

<p>Yeah&#8230; that's about as easy to figure out as &quot;What am I thinking about right now?&quot; I gotta be sceptical there's any real clues here, and not just random association. But the SCP itself is nicely written.</p>
<p>As an example, just going by the number thing, there are four men, the gordian knots branches into three lesser knots, with a line drawn from it into a wheel with four spokes, the wheel itself is circular that could be a zero, the pedestal could be seen as a 1 which gives you ten and this is why hiding pattern in numbers and things doesn't really work. Hell even that there was a chariot isn't noticeable unless you're told about it already. I guess the knot anchors the chariot so that when it is cut Zeus can take Jupiter on a sweet ride or something. Then they all fall apart into different body parts and decides to hang out in a gem.</p>

